(5154991, 749012, 83313, '<td valign="top">A really interesting contrast between the ice and flowers. Good eye for noticing this. <br/> <br/>It seems a little soft on the detail, so I looked at the file size. There is some excessive JPEG compression taking away some detail. Your file size is only 65k and you could have used up to 150k for this challenge. Compression kills detail. Always use the least compression you can get away with an still come in under challenge limits. Most image editors have that ability to adjust compression somewhere in the file save dialog. Here is how it works in Paintshop Pro, along with more explanation of compression, if is is of any help:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=742828" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/742828.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/742828.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/742828.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I also copied this into PaintShop Pro out of curiosity, and found that some easy and basic image adjsutments like levels, curves, saturation, contrast and sharpening really helped this to pop.</td>', 'A really interesting contrast between the ice and flowers. Good eye for noticing this.  It seems a little soft on the detail, so I looked at the file size. There is some excessive JPEG compression taking away some detail. Your file size is only 65k and you could have used up to 150k for this challenge. Compression kills detail. Always use the least compression you can get away with an still come in under challenge limits. Most image editors have that ability to adjust compression somewhere in the file save dialog. Here is how it works in Paintshop Pro, along with more explanation of compression, if is is of any help:  I also copied this into PaintShop Pro out of curiosity, and found that some easy and basic image adjsutments like levels, curves, saturation, contrast and sharpening really helped this to pop.', '2008-12-28 14:41:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5154995, 749631, 83313, '<td valign="top">The lighting plays on the items in a nice way, but the whole image seems a bit soft to me, and there is a visible tilt. I think a closer shot showing the light playing off that wedding dress would be visually interesting. Sorry to sound harsh, but I do see some nice potential here that you were trying to capture.</td>', 'The lighting plays on the items in a nice way, but the whole image seems a bit soft to me, and there is a visible tilt. I think a closer shot showing the light playing off that wedding dress would be visually interesting. Sorry to sound harsh, but I do see some nice potential here that you were trying to capture.', '2008-12-28 14:45:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5155000, 749613, 83313, '<td valign="top">For those who can''t afford a sports car? I need one of these!<br/> <br/>This is just so bizarre, that I have to give you one of my shoehorn awards for humor in a challenge. Enjoy. <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=737192" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/737192.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/737192.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/737192.jpg"/></a></td>', 'For those who can''t afford a sports car? I need one of these! This is just so bizarre, that I have to give you one of my shoehorn awards for humor in a challenge. Enjoy. ', '2008-12-28 14:49:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5155018, 749339, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the perspective, but overall it does not grab me. Maybe it is just a little to centered and static in composition for me. This is one of those shots that is actually good photography, but just does not seem to me to have the zing needed to stand out and get a high score in a challenge. <br/> <br/>Out of curiosity I pasted this into my image editor and some modest levels, curves and contrast adjustments caused this to lead my eye a little differently and helped the fine details pop out at me.</td>', 'I like the perspective, but overall it does not grab me. Maybe it is just a little to centered and static in composition for me. This is one of those shots that is actually good photography, but just does not seem to me to have the zing needed to stand out and get a high score in a challenge.  Out of curiosity I pasted this into my image editor and some modest levels, curves and contrast adjustments caused this to lead my eye a little differently and helped the fine details pop out at me.', '2008-12-28 14:56:58.000000', NULL, 1),
